Fillets: two stripe ends joined over a narrow face that pokes through the
ball's path, the blend holed there (mitcad#343).

The case: a rounding of radius 0.5 on three pieces of the edge between a
large torus Fo and a plane, the edge interrupted twice by a rod of the
solid, narrow strips of the rod's cylinder between the pieces (2.34 and
2.26 mm2). Past the pieces' ends the contacts on the plane run onto a
torus N of radius 0.6 that wraps the rod's foot, and patch 0932 ends the
walks before singular sections there: the ends' contacts on N lie on no
arc of the rod's strip C. In the file's body each pair of ends is one
blend over C. Over one strip the contact on N leaves N across C's edge and
comes back (the cut JoinOverNarrowFaces already makes); over the other it
stays on N all the way, and C pokes through the blend: the file's face
there has a hole bounded by a closed curve of 3.66 mm on the rod, the rod
keeping a lens of 0.888 mm2 inside it.

JoinOverNarrowFaces took C from the arc an end's contact on N ends on; where
no such arc's face holds both ends' vertices, C is now the face across an
edge of N that does (other than Fo, not tangent to N). Where the walked
contact never leaves N, the join is made when C's surface cuts the walked
blend in a closed curve and all of C lies beyond the walk's start section
(on it at the end's vertex): the walked blend replaces A's end as one
piece, from the start up to a section beyond C, the curve and B's end, cut
back to B's end piece there; PierceBlends then holes it, C keeping its
lens. Otherwise the stripes stay as they were.

On the design's replayed body the rounding, as the three pieces or with
the rod's two edges, builds in every order of its contours within 0.0033
mm3 of the file's change (7.5193 mm3), the rod's lens the file's; before,
two corners failed. Synthetic: a post on a plate, the edge round its foot
broken by two caps whose feet stay inside the rounding's contacts and that
poke through it, rounded with 0.5: the post's rounded foot with the caps
fused, within 7e-6 mm3, for 15 of 20 sizes (posts of radius 0.8 to 3,
caps 0.65 to 0.8; the other 5 fail as before); before, none of the 20
was right (invalid, wrong or failed).

Upstream: new.
